{
  "contract": "studio-unicode-ranges",
  "contractVersion": "pari-studio-request-v2",
  "rangeEncoding": "utf16-v1",
  "identitySeparator": "U+001F",
  "digest": "sha256 over UTF-8 bytes, lowercase hex",
  "notes": [
    "selection.start/end and protectedSpans.start/end are zero-based half-open UTF-16 code-unit offsets (AppKit NSRange).",
    "documentSha256 = sha256(documentText.encode('utf-8')); selectionSha256 and protectedSpanSha256 preimage = [rangeEncoding, documentSha256, str(start), str(end), text].join('\\u001f').encode('utf-8').",
    "No Unicode normalization is applied anywhere; NFC and NFD sources have different documentSha256.",
    "invalidCases entries may carry documentTextUnpairedSurrogate instead of documentText: the literal characters backslash-u-d-8-3-d encode one unpaired UTF-16 surrogate, which strict JSON readers (including Swift JSONSerialization) refuse to decode. Readers that cannot hold an unpaired surrogate must reconstruct the case from that field and assert only that the contract rejects it."
  ],
